WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.632
A source review becomes more useful when we quantify the problems.

00:00:03.632 --> 00:00:05.297
How many values are missing?

00:00:05.297 --> 00:00:07.272
How many fail a validation rule?

00:00:07.272 --> 00:00:10.247
How many duplicate groups appear after normalization?

00:00:10.247 --> 00:00:14.352
Are unusual values rare but plausible, or clearly impossible?

00:00:14.352 --> 00:00:19.692
Profiling gives you a baseline and helps you measure whether a cleaning step actually improves the dataset.

00:00:19.692 --> 00:00:25.127
Connect this idea to a product catalog standardizing categories and quarantining invalid rows.

00:00:25.127 --> 00:00:29.632
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:29.632 --> 00:00:35.992
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:35.992 --> 00:00:40.717
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:40.717 --> 00:00:45.840
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
